 "headline": "0 of 32 grafts beat the leader on celecoxib, amlodipine, scaffold_hop or perindopril",
 "the_mechanism_MEASURED": "Donors are ranked by the mean of the task's oracle over the molecules carrying each ring system, which is a RARITY-BIASED statistic. thiothixene's needed thioxanthene is carried by 6 molecules and ranks #3 of 2,402. celecoxib's and amlodipine's needed donor is plain BENZENE, carried by 203,732 molecules, whose mean is pinned near the corpus average: it ranks #382 and #1,043. A common ring can therefore never surface under this rule however useful it is in context. Same shape as the attachment-count '==' bug -- the ranking excludes the needed material by construction.",
 "also": "perindopril was diagnosed as needing EXCISION, not grafting, so a graft screen was always the wrong operation there and its -0.0220 is not evidence about the library.",
 "design_implication": "Mean-over-carriers is the right statistic for rare specific donors and the wrong one for common ones. A second lane is needed -- context-conditioned utility, or simply treating common rings as always-available -- but per the standing instruction no further infrastructure is built until an endpoint screen shows a scored gain, and only thiothixene has.",
